{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record-3/compare-packet-half1.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"part\\\"]),[print(k,[(c[\\\"id\\\"],c[\\\"line\\\"]) for a in v for c in a[\\\"cited_lines\\\"]]) for k,v in x[\\\"sets\\\"].items()]) for x in p if x[\\\"question\\\"]==\\\"Q2\\\" or (x[\\\"question\\\"]==\\\"Q3\\\" and x[\\\"part\\\"]==\\\"a\\\" and list(x[\\\"sets\\\"]))]'\"","aggregated_output":"\n Q2 a\nS1 [('B-003', \"**more than $411 billion** | estimate | source: Unnamed analysts (as reported by fool.com) | basis: Analysts' prediction as reported by the article; company-level annual revenue; no individual forecaster named | said: not stored | articles 36\"), ('B-038', \"**$411 billion** | estimate | source: Wall Street analysts (consensus estimate, unnamed) | basis: Wall Street analysts' estimate (consensus), as cited by the article | said: not stored | articles 28\")]\nS2 [('B-003', \"**more than $411 billion** | estimate | source: Unnamed analysts (as reported by fool.com) | basis: Analysts' prediction as reported by the article; company-level annual revenue; no individual forecaster named | said: not stored | articles 36\")]\nS3 [('T-094', \"Annual revenue: **more than $411 billion** | basis: Analysts' prediction as reported by the article; company-level annual revenue; no individual forecaster named | source as stored: Unnamed analysts (as reported by fool.com) | period as stored: Current fiscal year | said: not stored | article 36\")]\nS4 [('T-094', \"Annual revenue: **more than $411 billion** | basis: Analysts' prediction as reported by the article; company-level annual revenue; no individual forecaster named | source as stored: Unnamed analysts (as reported by fool.com) | period as stored: Current fiscal year | said: not stored | article 36\")]\nS5 [('T-093', \"revenu